//www.gutenberg.org/files/5682/5682-h/5682-h.htm"},{text:"The age of chivalry is gone. That of sophisters, economists, and calculators has succeeded.",author:"Edmund Burke",work:"Reflections on the Revolution in France",sourceUrl:"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/15679/15679-h/15679-h.htm"},{text:"You wanna fly, you got to give up the shit that weighs you down.",author:"Toni Morrison",work:"Song of Solomon",sourceUrl:"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/117657/song-of-solomon-by-toni-morrison/"},{text:"We accept the reality of the world with which we're presented.",author:"Christof",work:"The Truman Show",sourceUrl:"https://copioni.corrierespettacolo.it/wp-content/uploads/2016/12/NICCOL%20Andrew__The%20Truman%20show__null__null__Cinema__0.pdf"},{text:"I have become a question to myself.",author:"Augustine of Hippo",work:"Confessions, Book X, chapter 33",sourceUrl:"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/110110.htm"},{text:"The mind is its own place, and in itself\nCan make a Heaven of Hell, a Hell of Heaven.",author:"John Milton",work:"Paradise Lost, Book I",sourceUrl:"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/26/26-h/26-h.htm"},{text:"My own mind is my own church.",author:"Thomas Paine",work:"The Age of Reason, Part I",sourceUrl:"https://anthology.lib.virginia.edu/work/Paine/paine-age-reason"},{text:"Hell is other people.",author:"Jean-Paul Sartre",work:"No Exit",sourceUrl:"https://public.archive.wsu.edu/delahoyd/public_html/20th/sartre.noexit.html"},{text:"No man is an island, entire of itself; every man is a piece of the continent, a part of the main. If a clod be washed away by the sea, Europe is the less, as well as if a promontory were, as well as if a manor of thy friend’s or of thine own were: any man’s death diminishes me, because I am involved in mankind, and therefore never send to know for whom the bell tolls; it tolls for thee.",author:"John Donne",work:"Meditation XVII, Devotions upon Emergent Occasions",sourceUrl:"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/23772/23772-h/23772-h.htm"},{text:"Above all, don’t lie to yourself. The man who lies to himself, and listens to his own lie, comes to a point that he cannot distinguish the truth within him, or around him, and so loses all respect for himself and for others.",author:"Fyodor Dostoevsky",work:"The Brothers Karamazov",sourceUrl:"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/241840/the-brothers-karamazov-by-fyodor-dostoevsky-translated-by-richard-pevear-and-larissa-volokhonsky-introduction-by-malcolm-jones/"},{text:"I think that everyone should love life above everything in the world.",author:"Ivan Karamazov",work:"The Brothers Karamazov, Book V",sourceUrl:"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/241840/the-brothers-karamazov-by-fyodor-dostoevsky-translated-by-richard-pevear-and-larissa-volokhonsky-introduction-by-malcolm-jones/"},{text:"When you are old and grey and full of sleep,\nAnd nodding by the fire, take down this book,\nAnd slowly read, and dream of the soft look\nYour eyes had once, and of their shadows deep.",author:"W. B. Yeats",work:"“When You Are Old”",sourceUrl:"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/43283/when-you-are-old"},{text:"How dull it is to pause, to make an end,\nTo rust unburnish’d, not to shine in use!\n\nTo strive, to seek, to find, and not to yield.",author:"Alfred, Lord Tennyson",work:"“Ulysses”",sourceUrl:"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/45392/ulysses"}],S={Art:"I make no claims to artistry, as beauty is more than a matter of opinion. These are my modest attempts to capture it.",Music:"A violist by training, an actress by accident, and a firm believer that childhood ought to be filled with music. Here are a few notes from along the way.",Photos:"Photography began as a concession to laziness. Somewhere along the way, I traded the patience of painting for the immediacy of a shutter.",Writing:"A compilation of random thoughts, musings, and the occasional outburst. Mostly me thinking out loud on paper.",Pursuits:M,Work:"Consulting & Analysis \xb7 Law & Pub